The third chart with interesting numbers is the one that shows the number of new
installations (transaction type "Free") per device type.

---------------------------------
Device type    New installations
---------------------------------
iPhone         409k  (67%)
iPad           179k  (29%)
Desktop        18.5k  (3%)   (*1)
iPod touch     6.00k  (1%)   (*2)
Apple Vision   4             (*3)
Apple TV       1             (*4)
Apple Watch    1             (*5)
---------------------------------

(*1) I assume "Desktop" refers to installations made via the Mac App Store on
     macOS. Until 2024 I was not even aware that this distribution channel
     exists. With modern Xcode versions (e.g. Xcode 15.1) when you select the
     "Little Go" target you can see "Mac (designed for iPad)" as one of the
     destinations. However, the app must have been available on the Mac App
     Store for a lot longer, because the App Store Connect statistics show
     a number >0 already in 2011.
(*2) Version 2.0.0 of the app discontinued support for all existing iPod touch
     devices (Apple discontinued the last iPod touch device around 2016/2017),
     so numbers are not expected to grow anymore.
(*3) 08 February 2024    - 2 installations
     04 April 2024       - 1 installation
     06 April 2024       - 1 installation
(*4) 22 November 2023    - 1 installation
(*5) 03 June 2023        - 1 installation
